 ## Evidence limits
 
 This is a documentation contract and a reproducible paper review. It establishes no save file, no codec, no serializer, no round trip, no commit protocol, no recovery behaviour, no migration, no engine behaviour and no product answer. A named field is not an implemented field. The S0-07 citations are source review of a historical headless run with placeholder data on one Linux host; they establish the engine's JSON number handling and the placeholder envelope's shape, not any production projection, and the retained receipts were read, not rerun. The paper check proves internal consistency of two files against cited sources at one base; it cannot prove that a codec can produce these fields, that a restore rebuilds the right derived state, or that any open question's eventual answer is satisfiable within the reserved containers. No build, native or browser run, dependency change, asset admission, publication or save access occurred. Both browser proofs and their storage remain separate (TADR-004 line 42), and their tests cannot qualify this native persistence contract.
