-- [Q-P16](../../../BACKLOG.md#q-p16) (revival and unfinished-level interruption) is unanswered in both halves. This section adopts no candidate and no proposal. The interruption candidates P1 to P4 and the revival candidates R1 to R3 above are labelled pending Q-P16, and the invariant matrix and the five tabletop cases hold under each. Unresolved product choices, stated explicitly and gating dependent implementation: what health follows the standard revival; where the player is placed after it; whether an unfinished level leaves any durable record at all; if it does, which keys `run.interruption` carries; whether a forfeited level has a durable consequence beyond resuming at `run.checkpoint.next_entrance`; and whether an interruption may close a run. None of these is decided here, and no implementation may pick one from this section.
